      "HEPARIN potentiates ANTITHROMBIN III (does NOT bind calcium); GREEN cap; best for plasma biochemistry and blood gases; does not alter cell volume.",
      "Heparin is POOR for blood smears — blue background with Romanowsky stains, leukocyte and platelet clumping.",
      "TRISODIUM CITRATE 3.2%: chelates calcium REVERSIBLY; ratio 1 part citrate to 9 parts blood; BLUE cap; used for PT and APTT, ESR and transfusion.",
      "The 9:1 citrate ratio is critical — an underfilled tube FALSELY PROLONGS PT and APTT.",
      "SODIUM FLUORIDE is a glycolytic inhibitor preserving GLUCOSE; GREY cap. Without it glucose falls about 10% per hour.",
      "Double oxalate (Wintrobe): ammonium oxalate swells cells, potassium oxalate shrinks them — the 3:2 ratio balances cell volume.",
      "ACD and CPD are used for blood TRANSFUSION and banking; dextrose nourishes stored red cells.",
      "SERUM has NO FIBRINOGEN (consumed in the clot); PLASMA contains fibrinogen. Plasma yield is greater.",
      "HAEMOLYSIS falsely RAISES potassium, phosphorus, magnesium, AST, LDH and bilirubin, and interferes with colorimetric assays.",
